What is Edge AI?
Edge AI refers to the execution of artificial‑intelligence models directly on edge devices rather than in centralized cloud data‑centers. The approach combines compact, energy‑efficient silicon (such as neural‑processing units, tensor cores and specialized ASICs) with optimized software runtimes, allowing sophisticated deep‑learning models to run on devices that have limited power, compute and connectivity. Typical use‑cases include on‑device image classification, predictive maintenance analytics, voice‑activated assistants, autonomous navigation, and health‑monitoring wearables.
